# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_stale_base_nudge.py" "STALE BASE NUDGE GATE: PASS" "stale base nudge" "post-merge staleness nudge (the pre-conflict heads-up: Veripsa's collision detector compares CONCURRENTLY-open PRs and is BLIND to a change that ALREADY MERGED into the protected branch, so a file a PR is editing that a later landing touched only surfaces as a conflict at rebase/merge time — too late. github_rest.compare_changed_paths asks GitHub which files changed on the protected branch SINCE this PR's base [GET /compare/base...branch → filename STRINGS only, the patch body discarded → content-free]; render.stale_base_nudge_line intersects that with the PR's OWN changed files and, on an overlap, appends ONE advisory line to the ACTING PR's check SUMMARY ['main moved under you — rebase before merge to avoid a conflict']. Capped paths [≤3 + '+N more'], NON-fork only [the branch's other-landing paths are base-repo paths an external fork contributor must not see], FAIL-OPEN [any compare/render error logged + swallowed — an advisory add-on never breaks the customer check]; advisory [never blocks]; jargon-free. OFFLINE-tested: no Postgres — pure render fn + a fake _api on the thin REST method)" "post-merge staleness nudge (warns before rebase/merge that an ALREADY-MERGED change touched files your open PR also edits — the gap the concurrent-PR collision detector can't see; content-free, advisory, fail-open, non-fork)" 10
